1. You run a Spark query.

2. Databricks needs to read data.

3. Unity Catalog checks the External Table.

4. The External Table points to an External Location.

5. The External Location uses a Storage Credential.

6. The Storage Credential uses the Access Connector.

7. Azure verifies that the Access Connector has the
   Storage Blob Data Contributor role.

8. If authorized, Azure allows Databricks to read/write
   data in ADLS Gen2.